the-firm-as-one-program-28 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-28 = unlines (cons "- **C5** Risk bounds are invariants of the whole composed system ([C1: Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2], [P6], [P7])], [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)])." (cons "  The order ledger of hyperactivity v31 bounds filled position plus admitted outstanding orders and proves the bound over every admissible sequence of exchange events, including the interval during a rollout (hyperactivity v31 §10.10). That is the SEC's market access rule, 15c3-5, established as a theorem of the running system in place of a check performed system by system. Knight Capital lost about 440 million dollars in 45 minutes on 1 August 2012 because one of eight servers kept old code behind a repurposed flag. In one program the version on each server is a content identity, a flag that means two things in two versions is two different objects, and the rollout's invariant is proved over every interleaving. That failure cannot be constructed." nil))
